1
00:00:00,740 --> 00:00:04,660
So here we have the rampart tower, which is the tallest point.

2
00:00:05,140 --> 00:00:06,260
The town hall asked me for advice.

3
00:00:06,620 --> 00:00:08,920
What should be done? We had a medieval tower

4
00:00:10,320 --> 00:00:12,600
with a very unusual later transformation beneath it.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,760
At the top of the tower,

6
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:19,160
it was beginning to deteriorate,

7
00:00:19,220 --> 00:00:20,880
stones were starting to fall, and so on.

8
00:00:21,580 --> 00:00:24,320
So the elected officials asked me

9
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:27,600
what could be done to protect the tower.

10
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:31,860
Quite intuitively, I said the only thing we could do was to build a roof.

11
00:00:32,520 --> 00:00:35,380
So I designed a roof,

12
00:00:35,630 --> 00:00:39,740
combining a contemporary vision with respect for heritage.

13
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:41,840
Without trying to imitate the past,

14
00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:44,800
or crown it with fake historical elements.

15
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:48,720
Instead, the idea was to create contrast through a contemporary intervention,

16
00:00:49,460 --> 00:00:51,240
made of timber, with a crown-like structure,

17
00:00:51,480 --> 00:00:55,020
a conical roof,

18
00:00:55,860 --> 00:01:00,840
with a copper edge detail that gives it a more refined finish.

19
00:01:01,440 --> 00:01:04,620
Seen from below, it appears almost contemporary,

20
00:01:04,760 --> 00:01:08,480
because it almost seems roofless, but from farther away you clearly see the roof.

21
00:01:08,920 --> 00:01:10,980
In fact, it is visible from nearly every viewpoint.

22
00:01:11,260 --> 00:01:16,420
When you come down from the Saint-Antonin road, it suddenly appears, yet still feels balanced.

23
00:01:16,420 --> 00:01:20,820
That is also why the Architects of Historic Buildings approved — and even appreciated — the proposal.

24
00:01:22,180 --> 00:01:29,280
So in the end, this remains what I consider a contemporary intervention.

25
00:01:30,300 --> 00:01:35,080
An interesting aspect of the story is that architecture projects are usually very slow.

26
00:01:35,880 --> 00:01:39,380
Here, however, it was built in a workshop by an excellent local craftsman.

27
00:01:39,900 --> 00:01:42,540
So the architect and the craftsman worked closely together.

28
00:01:43,100 --> 00:01:46,500
We are adding something new, but in harmony with the existing structure.

29
00:01:47,340 --> 00:01:50,700
Harmony can also come through contrast, rather than imitation.

30
00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:55,260
Through contrast, we highlight what was already there.

31
00:01:55,750 --> 00:01:58,380
And that does not prevent restoration itself.

32
00:01:58,490 --> 00:01:59,200
We did restore it.

33
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:02,420
But we also offer another perspective.

34
00:02:03,380 --> 00:02:08,940
We provide new ways of reading and understanding this existing building.

35
00:02:09,240 --> 00:02:11,360
And we bring it into the contemporary era.